# OS_LAB2

This repository contains my implementation of Project 2 for the Operating Systems Lab. The project focuses on understanding and extending the system call mechanism within the xv6 operating system kernel. The modifications include altering how syscall arguments are passed by reading them directly from registers instead of the process stack. Additionally, several new system calls were implemented from scratch. These include a file duplication tool, a process family tracker to retrieve parent, child, and sibling relationships, a kernel-level grep for searching specific keywords within files, and a priority setter to modify process scheduling behavior similar to the Linux nice command. User-space test programs were also developed to validate the functionality of these kernel-level additions
